perfect parent. And there's a lot of pressure to monitor and set them up for success. And I completely understand that. But my general takeaway, honestly, is that most people are probably doing a good job. If you care about your kids, you know, the fact that you're asking me this question, for instance, is already revealing that you're an engaged parent who cares about your child's well-being. And a lot of the, you know, a lot of the outcomes that we care about, I think that's a pretty good predictor of it. And, you know, the other part truly is that, like, you as a parent are also a human being, you know, and there are costs and benefits to you. And you do need to think about yourself. The family is this, you know, it has to be in some degree of harmony. And so if you find yourself really anxious and really upset about some of the choices

