00:34:29.000 --> 00:35:08.000
And so what I try to do as much as possible is get the kids. kids together because I just think that my, like, I'm not good on it. And every time I try to pretend something with my five-year-old, he tells me I'm doing it wrong anyway. So, you know, why am I bothering? But I think, you know, there's a lot of pressure to be, you know, be like their zany playfriend. And the other thing, you know, that I want to mention is that I think we have this conceptualization of a perfect childhood as one that is always positive. Like we, we, we, there are no negative experiences. They're not bored. They're entertained. They're learning. all the time. They're really happy. And I think those are good goals. But I also think that that's not

